IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- domain.l4: the shared nouns for the encoding of the Regulation of Engagement in Work on
-- Refrigeration or Air-Conditioning Systems Law 5785-2025 and its Fees Regulations.
-- Written once by the SURVEYOR; DECLARE only, no rule and no #EVAL.  Encoders IMPORT it and
-- never edit it: a noun that is missing goes in the encoder's FRAGMENT as a "nouns request".
--
-- The test for membership is whether a witness of ordinary competence could testify to the
-- fact.  What a fact MEANS under the Law (is the licence in force, is the work covered, which
-- row of a Schedule applies) is a rule, and belongs to the group that encodes the section.
-- Facts the Law leaves to an official's opinion (fitness, recognition, special circumstances)
-- are INPUTS carried in a group's own records, not fields here.
-- English names follow the TERMINOLOGY table in phase1/PLAN.md.  Quotations are copied by script.

-- The definitions of s.2, copied by script from inputs/law.wiki.
-- src:41 | {{ח:ת}} בחוק זה –
-- src:42 | {{ח:ת|סוג=הגדרה}} ”אגף להכשרה מקצועית“ – אגף להכשרה מקצועית ולפיתוח כוח אדם האחראי למתן תעודות מקצוע כמשמעותן {{ח:חיצוני|חוק שירות התעסוקה#פרק 3|בפרק שלישי לחוק שירות התעסוקה, התשי״ט–1959}};
-- src:43 | {{ח:ת|סוג=הגדרה}} ”בעל רישיון“ – בעל רישיון לבצע עבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר לפי הוראות חוק זה;
-- src:44 | {{ח:ת|סוג=הגדרה}} ”חוק ההנדסאים והטכנאים המוסמכים“ – {{ח:חיצוני|חוק ההנדסאים והטכנאים המוסמכים|חוק ההנדסאים והטכנאים המוסמכים, התשע״ג–2012}};
-- src:45 | {{ח:ת|סוג=הגדרה}} ”חוק החשמל“ – {{ח:חיצוני|חוק החשמל|חוק החשמל, התשי״ד–1954}};
-- src:46 | {{ח:ת|סוג=הגדרה}} ”חוק העונשין“ – {{ח:חיצוני|חוק העונשין|חוק העונשין, התשל״ז–1977}};
-- src:47 | {{ח:ת|סוג=הגדרה}} ”המועצה“ – המועצה המייעצת שמונתה לפי {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 20|סעיף 20}};
-- src:48 | {{ח:ת|סוג=הגדרה}} ”מערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר“, ”מערכת“ – מערכת, מיתקן או מוצר, שייעודם הרחקת חום אל מחוץ לחומר או לחלל נתון, באמצעות קרר;
-- src:49 | {{ח:ת|סוג=הגדרה}} ”מפקח“ – עובד המשרד שהשר הסמיכו לפי {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 30|סעיף 30(א)}};
-- src:50 | {{ח:ת|סוג=הגדרה}} ”המפקח הבכיר“ – מפקח שהשר הסמיכו למפקח בכיר לפי {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 34|סעיף 34(א)}};
-- src:51 | {{ח:ת|סוג=הגדרה}} ”מרשם ההנדסאים והטכנאים המוסמכים“ – כמשמעותו {{ח:חיצוני|חוק ההנדסאים והטכנאים המוסמכים#סעיף 17|בסעיף 17 לחוק ההנדסאים והטכנאים המוסמכים}};
-- src:52 | {{ח:ת|סוג=הגדרה}} ”המשרד“ – משרד העבודה;
-- src:53 | {{ח:ת|סוג=הגדרה}} ”עבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר“ – ביצוע פעולה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר שהיא מסוג הפעולות הקבועות {{ח:פנימי|תוספת 1|בתוספת הראשונה}};
-- src:54 | {{ח:ת|סוג=הגדרה}} ”קרר“ (refrigerant) – גז או נוזל המאפשר הרחקת חום;
-- src:55 | {{ח:ת|סוג=הגדרה}} ”רישיון“ – כל אחד מסוגי הרישיונות שלהלן, לביצוע עבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר:
-- src:56 | {{ח:תתת|(1)}} רישיון דרגה 1;
-- src:57 | {{ח:תתת|(2)}} רישיון דרגה 2;
-- src:58 | {{ח:תתת|(3)}} רישיון דרגה 3;
-- src:59 | {{ח:ת|סוג=הגדרה}} ”רישיון דרגה 1“ – רישיון לביצוע עבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר שתפוקת הקירור שלה עד 18 קילו־ואט;
-- src:60 | {{ח:ת|סוג=הגדרה}} ”רישיון דרגה 2“ – רישיון לביצוע עבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר שתפוקת הקירור שלה עד 70 קילו־ואט;
-- src:61 | {{ח:ת|סוג=הגדרה}} ”רישיון דרגה 3“ – רישיון לביצוע עבודה בכל מערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר;
-- src:62 | {{ח:ת|סוג=הגדרה}} ”הרשם“ – מי שמונה לפי {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 19|סעיף 19}};
-- src:63 | {{ח:ת|סוג=הגדרה}} ”תעודת גמר“ – אחת מאלה:
-- src:64 | {{ח:תתת|(1)}} תעודה שהנפיק האגף להכשרה מקצועית המעידה על סיום לימודי קירור ומיזוג אוויר ומעבר בהצלחה של בחינה שערך האגף להכשרה מקצועית, הכוללת בחינה עיונית ובחינה מעשית;
-- src:65 | {{ח:תתת|(2)}} תעודה שהנפיק משרד החינוך המעידה על סיום בהצלחה של לימודים במגמת בקרת אקלים;
-- src:66 | {{ח:ת|סוג=הגדרה}} ”השר“ – שר העבודה.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Parties: the offices and capacities that act in a regulative rule (s.2 and the sections
-- named in each constructor's comment).  Offices are parties, individuals are not.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref s.2 definitions (src:41-66)
@desc The offices and capacities that act, or are acted on, in the Law's duties, powers and prohibitions; an office is a party, a named individual is not
DECLARE Party IS ONE OF
    `a person`                                -- anyone: the subject of "no person shall", s.3(a), s.4
    `the applicant`                           -- s.5(a)
    `the licensee`                            -- s.2, holder of a licence
    `the operator`                            -- s.18(c)
    `the Registrar`                           -- s.2, s.19
    `the Minister`                            -- s.2, the Minister of Labour
    `the Council`                             -- s.2, s.20
    `the Council chair`                       -- s.20(1)
    `a Council member`                        -- s.20
    `the Director of the Training Division`   -- s.7
    `an inspector`                            -- s.2, s.30
    `the senior inspector`                    -- s.2, s.34
    `a testing body`                          -- s.33
    `a tester`                                -- s.33, the person who does auxiliary tests
    `an expert`                               -- s.33
    `the Commissioner`                        -- s.41(a), the senior Ministry employee for Chapter 6
    `the violator`                            -- s.42(a)
    `the Ministry`                            -- s.2, the Ministry of Labour
    `the court`                               -- s.56, the Magistrates' Court on appeal
    `the Training Division`                   -- s.2; reg.4 of the Fees Regulations binds the Division itself
    `the Director General of the Ministry of Labour` -- reg.3(b) of the Fees Regulations
    `the occupier of the place`               -- ss.31(3), 37(b): consents, may refuse, may withdraw consent
    `the orderer of the work`                 -- s.14: may demand to see the licence
    `a subcommittee of the Council`           -- s.26(b)

@ref s.2 definitions (src:41-66)
@desc Whether a person is an individual or a corporation; the Third Schedule, s.41(b) and s.57(e) answer differently for each
DECLARE `Person kind` IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `a corporation`

@desc A person, identified by a reference; equality of the reference field is identity, never equality of the whole record
DECLARE Person HAS
    `reference for the person` IS A STRING @desc Any stable identifier for the person, such as a national or company number; two records with the same reference are the same person
    `kind of person` IS A `Person kind` @desc Whether the person is an individual or a corporation

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Licences (s.2, s.8, s.9, s.10, s.11)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref s.2 definitions (src:41-66)
@desc The three kinds of licence; the kind decides which cooling systems the licensee may work on (grade 1 up to 18 kW, grade 2 up to 70 kW, grade 3 any system)
DECLARE `Licence kind` IS ONE OF
    `grade 1 licence`    -- s.2: a system whose cooling capacity is up to 18 kW
    `grade 2 licence`    -- s.2: a system whose cooling capacity is up to 70 kW
    `grade 3 licence`    -- s.2: any cooling system

@desc A licence as the register of s.11 records it: facts about one licence; whether it is in force on a day is a rule (s.8, s.9, s.10) and is not a field
DECLARE Licence HAS
    `the holder` IS A Person @desc The person to whom the licence was granted
    `the kind of licence` IS A `Licence kind` @desc Grade 1, 2 or 3; a temporary licence under s.9 is a grade 3 licence
    `a temporary licence under section 9` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the licence is a foreign expert's temporary licence under s.9
    `granted on` IS A DATE @desc The day the licence was granted
    `renewed on` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc The days on which the licence was renewed, oldest first; empty if never renewed
    `validity ends on, as recorded` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc The last day of validity the register shows; NOTHING if no end is recorded
    `revoked on` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc The day the licence was revoked under s.10; NOTHING if it has not been
    `suspended from` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc The first day of a suspension under s.10; NOTHING if never suspended
    `suspended until` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc The last day of a suspension; NOTHING if there is no end fixed (for example a suspension until final judgment under s.10(b)) or no suspension

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Cooling systems and work on them (s.2, First Schedule, s.63, Fourth Schedule)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref s.2 definitions (src:41-66)
@desc A refrigerant, identified by the designation printed on the unit or in the Fourth Schedule; whether it is a listed flammable refrigerant is a rule of s.63, not a field
DECLARE Refrigerant HAS
    `designation` IS A STRING @desc The designation without the leading R and without any direction marks, for example 290, 600a, 1234yf or E170; compare it as plain text
    `use of the refrigerant is permitted by law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the use of this refrigerant is permitted under any enactment other than this Law (the proviso of s.63(a)(1) is said of the refrigerant, so a system with two refrigerants can have one lawful and one not)

@ref s.2 definitions (src:41-66)
@desc A refrigeration or air-conditioning system, installation or product that removes heat by means of a refrigerant
DECLARE `Cooling system` HAS
    `cooling capacity in kilowatts` IS A NUMBER @desc The cooling output in kW; s.2 reads "up to 18" and "up to 70" as inclusive
    `refrigerants` IS A LIST OF Refrigerant @desc Every refrigerant the system operates with; empty if none is recorded; a system with two refrigerants lists both

@desc Whether a piece of work is installation (First Schedule Part A) or maintenance (Part B)
DECLARE `Job kind` IS ONE OF
    `an installation job`    -- First Schedule, Part A
    `a maintenance job`      -- First Schedule, Part B

@desc One piece of work done on one cooling system; which First Schedule activity it is, and whether it is "work" at all under s.2, are rules of the First Schedule group
DECLARE `Work item` HAS
    `performed by` IS A Person @desc The person who did the work
    `the kind of job` IS A `Job kind` @desc Installation or maintenance
    `the system` IS A `Cooling system` @desc The system the work was done on
    `date performed` IS A DATE @desc The day the work was done

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Applicants and what they hold (ss.5 to 9, Second Schedule)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

@desc A final certificate or qualifying certificate named in s.2 and in column A of the Second Schedule; the grade, where the certificate states one, is part of the constructor
DECLARE Certificate IS ONE OF
    `a Training Division certificate of grade 1`                         -- Second Schedule: grade 1 certificate
    `a Training Division certificate of grade 2`                         -- grade 2 certificate
    `a Training Division certificate of grade 3`                         -- grade 3 certificate (named for completeness; no row asks for it)
    `a Training Division certificate with no grade stated`               -- "a certificate in refrigeration and air-conditioning studies from the Training Division"
    `a certificate of the Training Division vocational school for youth` -- Part B row 5 (2)
    `a Ministry of Education climate-control certificate of 3 study units`
    `a Ministry of Education climate-control certificate of 5 study units`

@desc A stretch of days in which a person worked on cooling systems, for the experience tests of the Second Schedule (counted backwards from the application day, a count s.10 of the Interpretation Law does not cover)
DECLARE `Period of work on cooling systems` HAS
    `first day of the period` IS A DATE @desc First day worked
    `last day of the period` IS A DATE @desc Last day worked, inclusive

@desc A person who applies for a licence or renewal (s.5(a)) and the facts about them that ss.6, 7 and 9 and the Second Schedule ask for
DECLARE Applicant HAS
    `the person` IS A Person @desc The applicant as a person
    `of full age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the applicant is an adult under the general law (s.6(a)(1)); the age threshold is not stated in this Law
    `an Israeli citizen` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the applicant is an Israeli citizen (s.6(a)(2))
    `an Israeli resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the applicant is a resident of Israel (s.6(a)(2))
    `record of offences` IS A `Record of offences` @desc Convictions and pending proceedings against the applicant (s.6(a)(3))
    `licences held` IS A LIST OF Licence @desc Every licence the applicant holds or held, with its recorded dates
    `certificates held` IS A LIST OF Certificate @desc Every certificate the applicant holds, as listed in column A of the Second Schedule
    `registered as a certified technician in refrigeration and air conditioning` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if registered in the register of technicians and practical engineers, branch and section of refrigeration and air conditioning, as a technician (s.6(a)(4)(b), Second Schedule Part B rows 2 and 6)
    `registered as a certified practical engineer in refrigeration and air conditioning` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if so registered as a practical engineer (Second Schedule Part C rows 2 and 7)
    `completed a study programme that includes the complement course` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the applicant completed a programme that includes the complement course (Second Schedule Part B row 2, Part C row 2)
    `registered as an engineer in the mechanical branch` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if registered as an engineer in the mechanical branch under the Engineers and Architects Law (Second Schedule Part C row 8)
    `periods of work on cooling systems` IS A LIST OF `Period of work on cooling systems` @desc The stretches in which the applicant worked on cooling systems, for the experience rows of the Second Schedule
    `holds a valid electrician licence of a kind listed in the Electricity Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the applicant holds a valid licence of a kind named in regulation 7, paragraphs (1) to (7), of the Electricity (Licences) Regulations (s.7(a))
    `holds a valid working-at-height approval` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the applicant holds a valid approval that they were instructed in working at height under regulations 5 and 6 of the Work at Height Regulations (s.7(b))

@desc Convictions and pending proceedings against a person, as facts; whether an offence makes the person unfit is the opinion of the Registrar, the Minister or the Council appointer, an input, not a field
DECLARE `Record of offences` HAS
    `convicted of a criminal offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if convicted of any criminal offence
    `convicted of a disciplinary offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if convicted of any disciplinary offence (ss.21 and 23)
    `charged with a criminal offence and no final judgment yet` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if an indictment is pending with no final judgment
    `a disciplinary complaint is pending with no final judgment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if a disciplinary complaint (the s.21 "complaint") is pending with no final judgment

@desc An application for a licence or its renewal (s.5)
DECLARE Application HAS
    `the applicant` IS AN Applicant @desc Who applies
    `the kind of licence sought` IS A `Licence kind` @desc Grade 1, 2 or 3
    `an application to renew` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the application is to renew an existing licence (s.5(a), s.8)
    `an application for a temporary licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the application is for a foreign expert's temporary licence (s.9)
    `the day of the application` IS A DATE @desc The day the application was made; the experience tests of the Second Schedule count backwards from it

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Calendar input (Interpretation Law s.10(c))
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

@desc The days of rest, recess or holiday that s.10(c) of the Interpretation Law refers to; one input, named the same way by every group; never computed
DECLARE `Calendar of rest days` HAS
    `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc Every day that is a day of rest, recess or holiday under an enactment, for the years the question touches; a list that runs out is a calendar that answers "not a rest day"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Violations (the Third Schedule; Chapter 6)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The Third Schedule, column A, items (1) to (7), copied by script from inputs/law.wiki.
-- src:706 | {{ח:תת|(1)}} עוסק שביצע עבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר בלי שיש בידו רישיון כלל, בניגוד להוראות {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 3|סעיף 3(א)}};
-- src:709 | {{ח:תת|(2)}} ביצע עבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר בלי שיש בידו רישיון מהסוג המתאים לביצוע פעולה באותה מערכת, בניגוד להוראות {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 3|סעיף 3(א)}};
-- src:712 | {{ח:תת|(3)}} פרסם עצמו כבעל רישיון בלי שיש בידו רישיון או פרסם עצמו כבעל רישיון מסוג מסוים בלי שיש בידו רישיון מאותו סוג, בניגוד להוראות {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 4|סעיף 4}};
-- src:715 | {{ח:תת|(4)}} בעל רישיון שביצע התקנה של מערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר בלי לבצע בדיקת אטימות לצנרת חומר הקירור בהתאם להוראות הקבועות בפרק הבדיקות בתקן ישראלי ת״י 994 חלק 4 – מזגני אוויר: התקנה, בניגוד להוראת {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 13|סעיף 13}};
-- src:718 | {{ח:תת|(5)}} מפעיל שהפעיל אדם אחר בביצוע עבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר בלי שיש בידי אותו אדם רישיון כלל, בניגוד להוראות {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 18|סעיף 18(א)}};
-- src:721 | {{ח:תת|(6)}} מפעיל שהפעיל אדם אחר בביצוע עבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר בלי שיש בידי אותו אדם רישיון מהסוג המתאים לביצוע עבודה באותה מערכת, בניגוד להוראות {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 18|סעיף 18(א)}};
-- src:724 | {{ח:תת|(7)}} לא מסר מסמך לפי דרישת מפקח שניתנה לפי {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 31|סעיף 31(2)}}.

@ref Third Schedule, items (1) to (7) (src:706-724)
@desc The seven violations the Third Schedule prices; the interface between the groups that decide that a violation occurred (ss.3, 4, 13, 18, 31) and the group that prices it
DECLARE `Listed violation` IS ONE OF
    `work with no licence at all`                                 -- item (1), s.3(a)
    `work without a licence of the kind appropriate to the system` -- item (2), s.3(a)
    `advertising as licensed without the licence or the kind`      -- item (3), s.4
    `installation without the tightness test of the piping`        -- item (4), s.13
    `engaging a person who had no licence at all`                  -- item (5), s.18(a)
    `engaging a person without a licence of the appropriate kind`  -- item (6), s.18(a)
    `failing to give a document an inspector demanded`             -- item (7), s.31(2)

@desc One act that breached a listed provision; carries what ss.41 to 57 ask first
DECLARE Violation HAS
    `the violator` IS A Person @desc Who committed the act
    `the listed violation` IS A `Listed violation` @desc Which Third Schedule item the act breached
    `reference for the act` IS A STRING @desc Identifies the act itself; two violations with the same reference are one act, which s.55 allows only one sanction for
    `date of the act` IS A DATE @desc The day the act was committed

@desc One reading of the consumer price index (the Law's "index"); ss.47(b) and the Fees Regulations' regulation 3 both update amounts by it
DECLARE `Price index reading` HAS
    `year of the index` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year the reading is for
    `month of the index` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar month, 1 to 12
    `published on` IS A DATE @desc The day the reading was published; an index "known on" a day is the latest reading published by then
    `value of the index` IS A NUMBER @desc The index value on the base the publisher uses
